$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM c) The mixture of compound 11 (20 mg, 0.10 mmol),
2-chloro-4-(methylsulfonyl)benzoic acid (12) (35 mg, 0.15 mmol), HATU (76
mg, 0.20 mmol), HOAt (20 mg, 0.15 mmol), and DIPEA (99 µL, 0.60 mmol) in
anhydrous DCM (2 mL) was stirred at room temperature overnight. Water was
added and the mixture was extracted with DCM. The combined organic phase
was washed with brine, dried over anhydrous sodium sulfate, and
concentrated. The residue was purified on a silica gel column with
petroleum ether/ethyl acetate (1/2) as the eluent. Vismodegib (35 mg,
84%). The spectral data were in accordance with those reported in the
previous literature.10
